                                                              "summary":  "Ron Baron\u0027s mutual funds have compounded client wealth since the early 1980s, with outsized returns driven by early, concentrated bets on Tesla and SpaceX held through years of market ridicule. Starting from $10 million with George Soros as his sole client, Baron Capital grew to roughly $70 billion in AUM. The piece spotlights Baron\u0027s conviction-based, decade-long holding philosophy as the core engine of his returns, distinct from momentum or quant strategies. Brown frames Baron as a case study in the rare ability to stay right when the crowd is loudly wrong.",
